# ─── Pink Binder environment reference ───────────────────────────────────────
#
# We manage secrets in Vercel, not in a shared root `.env.local`.
#
# ## Local setup (default)
#
# 1. Install the Vercel CLI and log in: https://vercel.com/docs/cli
# 2. Link each app you work on from its directory:
#      cd apps/landing && vercel link
#      cd apps/blog    && vercel link
# 3. Pull env for that project into the app folder:
#      cd apps/<app> && vercel env pull .env.local
# 4. Restart dev after pulling: `bun dev` or `bun dev:blog`
#
# Next.js loads `apps/<app>/.env.local` automatically when you run that app.
# Optional repo-root `.env.local` is still merged by `scripts/with-env.mjs` for
# legacy overrides only — prefer Vercel per-project env going forward.
#
# Server-side by default. Prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_ for browser-visible values.
#
# ─── Shared marketplace keys (usually on landing; duplicate on blog if needed) ─
#
# ETSY_SHOP_ID=
# ETSY_KEYSTRING=
# ETSY_SECRET=
# EBAY_APP_ID=
# EBAY_CLIENT_SECRET=
# EBAY_VERIFICATION_TOKEN=
# EBAY_ACCOUNT_DELETION_ENDPOINT=
# EBAY_DEBUG=1
# WHATNOT_USERNAME=thepinkbinder
# WHATNOT_USER_AGENT=
# WHATNOT_SCRAPE_CACHE_TTL_MS=60000
# LIVE_SHOWS_SOURCE_URL=
# LIVE_SHOWS_SOURCE_TOKEN=
#
# ─── Site URLs (client-side) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LANDING_URL=https://pinkbinder.shop
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BLOG_URL=https://pinkbinder.blog
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SHOWS_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=60000
#
# ─── Analytics (per app, client-side) ────────────────────────────────────────
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GTM_ID=GTM-XXXXXXX
# GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=replace-with-search-console-token
#
# ─── Blog / data pipeline (blog Vercel project) ──────────────────────────────
#
# Vercel Blob — auto-provisioned when Blob storage is enabled on the blog project.
# Used by `bun --filter @repo/data transform` (pull from apps/blog).
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=
